WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.632
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.632 --> 00:00:03.810
- [Kelly] I love this. Is that quartz?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.770
- [Chris] Uh, it is.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.603
- It's quartz?
- Thank you.

00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:06.690
- I love quartz.
- Thank you.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.930
- Somebody told me-
- Bringing in the good juju.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.930
- I know. Somebody told me
about quartz a long time ago

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.430
and I was like, "Look, I don't
know if it works or not,"

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.500
but I put it out by
the moon, I load it up.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.179
I do all the things, just in case.

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:16.012
- I mean, I'm wearing all the-

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:19.200
- I know. Just in case,
jade it up. I do it all.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.550
I don't know if it's real or not but,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.900
- It makes me feel good.
- Why not? Why not?

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.770
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.603
- It is if we say it is.

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:25.584
- Yeah, it is if I say it is, as well.

00:00:25.584 --> 00:00:26.417
(both laughing)

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.140
- We were just talking about Graceland.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.020
You live in Tennessee, right?

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:29.853
- I do, I do.

00:00:29.853 --> 00:00:31.080
- Have you ever been to Graceland?

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.560
- I have! As a matter of fact, I went,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.023
when I was on the show, we went,

00:00:37.023 --> 00:00:38.626
'the show', "Idol",

00:00:38.626 --> 00:00:40.200
we went to Graceland

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.880
- Because it was the week,
- Oh!

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.942
- That was the week I got voted off

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:45.150
- (laughs) doing Elvis.
- No.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.670
- And it was the week I was most proud of!

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.100
I did "Suspicious Minds",
I'm like, "I know this jam."

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.770
And, yeah,

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.603
that was, um,

00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:55.170
so I got to meet Priscilla

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.277
- And Lisa Marie
- Wow!

00:00:56.277 --> 00:00:59.400
- And it was an incredible
experience, yeah.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.900
- Oh, my God, I've missed that.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.310
- A couple times. And we're
actually getting ready

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.490
to perform there. They
have a venue there now.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.630
- Oh really?
- Yeah.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.800
- Oh, wow. See, I gotta go check it out.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.030
I've lived in Nashville for, like, ever,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.481
- I can't believe you've never been.

00:01:10.481 --> 00:01:11.314
- 12 years, I never, I never.

00:01:11.314 --> 00:01:14.070
- I can, I work a lot.
- (both laugh)

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.660
- But I just, yeah, I never made it there

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.160
and I don't know how I did it.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.930
But, I love that you live in Nashville.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.412
It's such a great place to work and live.

00:01:22.412 --> 00:01:23.550
- It's a good place
- Yes, yes.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.260
- For musicians
- Yes. Very much so.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.550
- of all different genres, I feel like.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.410
- Yeah. I have so many friends there

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.970
and we never see each other. (laughs)

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.040
- Oh, my God! That's the
biggest joke here for me.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.360
Everybody's like, "What do
you do in your off time?"

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.860
And I was like, "Oh, that's a cute term."

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.230
- Yeah, I'm in bed by nine o'clock, easy.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.587
- 'Cause when you're
a parent, you're like,

00:01:38.587 --> 00:01:40.800
"Um, I get home from
work and then I parent,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.410
so that's what I do. I'm so cool."

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.420
But speaking of being a parent,

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.520
everybody has had a rough few years.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.980
Especially with mental illness.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.420
And I know you lost your
stepdaughter, Hannah,

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.190
- to suicide.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.240
- How have you been doing?

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.280
How's your wife been doing?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.900
It was right before the tour.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.220
I lost my mom to cancer,

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.420
- Oh my God.
- And then

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.073
- Exactly one week later,
lost my daughter to suicide.

00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:07.560
And it's been,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.600
- Geez!
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:10.530
- It's been a learning,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.723
I mean, for all of us.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:17.283
I think the hardest thing that I found,

00:02:18.482 --> 00:02:20.640
because I dealt with
both very differently,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.700
processed both losses very differently.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.290
But, I think the hardest thing,

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.320
and the common denominator
in both is the guilt.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.037
The, "I wish I would have said this,"

00:02:30.037 --> 00:02:31.477
"I wish I would have done this,"

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:33.547
"I wish I would have called more,"

00:02:33.547 --> 00:02:34.737
"I wish I would've-"

00:02:36.494 --> 00:02:37.327
- [Kelly] All the thoughts.

00:02:37.327 --> 00:02:38.160
- All the things.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.820
"Oh, this would be a time
that I would call my mom,"

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.437
Or this would be a time that I would be,

00:02:44.437 --> 00:02:47.430
"Hey, Mom, I'm on 'The Kelly
Clarkson Show'." You know?

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.273
And so,

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.670
those moments of

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.200
the guilt is the hardest

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.490
because you can't do anything about it.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.140
And there's always gonna be reminders

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.360
of what you could have done or whatever.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.780
And I tend to beat
myself up a lot over it.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.760
But it's been, uh,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.250
it's been a very healing time

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.083
in our house,

00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:09.553
and we dealt with it
in a very healthy way.

00:03:09.553 --> 00:03:11.013
And our kids, you know,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.620
were part of

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.553
the burial.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.180
And watching my kids,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.370
I'm kind of going off the topic here,

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.513
but we did a natural
burial that she wanted.

00:03:26.155 --> 00:03:28.950
And my kids, I don't know if you know,

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.490
but basically it's

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:32.850
a basket,

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:33.693
so to speak,

00:03:35.166 --> 00:03:37.916
and it's a place in Tennessee
that does natural burials

00:03:39.178 --> 00:03:40.110
and we all had shovels

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.700
and we all got to cover

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:44.543
the basket.

00:03:44.543 --> 00:03:47.400
And seeing my kids do that
and seeing them process,

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.930
it was a very

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.583
heavy, magical,

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.650
it's hard to explain.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.247
But seeing them process that,

00:03:56.247 --> 00:03:57.358
- I've never heard of
- and being a part of it,

00:03:57.358 --> 00:03:58.590
- that kind of burial.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.583
- It's incredible.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.100
And it was,

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.230
- It seems kind of healing
- very healing

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.210
- Healing to be a part of that

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:07.350
and see them be a part of that

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.000
and have everyone there

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.938
be a part of it,

00:04:10.938 --> 00:04:13.380
it's not just sitting on the outside.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.510
Everyone was involved and it was very

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.940
- healing, yeah. Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.500
- Well, you're performing a song

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.180
off your album, "Dearly Beloved",

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.180
and this is your first release,
is it on your own label?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.580
- Yes.
- How does that feel?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.380
- Very liberating.
- Yeah, freeing, yeah.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.880
- To not have anybody's voice but your own

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.370
and your tight circle of producers

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.920
and writers that you work with.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.600
I wasn't chasing anything,

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.770
I wasn't trying to write a
radio song, or this or that.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.322
It was just, "let's write,"

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:52.230
and that was such a gratifying experience.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.370
- I love that for you
- I'm the most

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.920
- Proud of this record
because of it, you know?

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.840
- Oh man, I love that
for you, as an artist.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:58.770
- Thank you.
- That's really cool.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.060
That freedom is cool.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.927
- Thank you so much, Chris.
- Thank you for having me.

00:05:01.927 --> 00:05:03.894
- Thank you for coming.
- (audience cheering)

00:05:03.894 --> 00:05:05.056
- Time for a break everybody.

00:05:05.056 --> 00:05:06.780
Daughtry's latest album
is "Dearly Beloved".

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:09.480
You can get it right now
wherever you get your music.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.640
And stick around because
Daughtry is performing

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.473
later in the show with a beard.

